{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1101991-dr-facilier-as-a-mage-how-it-could-be-done","id":1101991,"title":"Dr. Facilier as a mage, how it could be done?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-09T08:19:30-07:00","id":1101991,"title":"Dr. Facilier as a mage, how it could be done?","content":"So the other I was watching some random videos when I found this one from a Disney movie named The Princess and the frog. The bad guy there is Dr. Facilier a voodo wizard (priest?) known as The Shadow Man (and as you can see in the video it is quite obvious why).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yZAY-78zhmw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yZAY-78zhmw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yZAY-78zhmw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yZAY-78zhmw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So then I was thinking, how can you make a character for Mage with that set of powers?<br /> <br /> The first thing I thought was that he was obviously a Dreamspeaker. Possibly with spheres on Spirit and Life (or perhaps Time or Mind to pull off the card reading thing).<br /> <br /> But the next thing was, how could you do the shadow-like spirits that help him in the movie? Not to mention the Friend on the other side. Are there spirits like that in the World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> What do you think? Could he be from a another group of mages? What Spheres would be good for the guy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T08:56:00-07:00","id":1101999,"title":"","content":"Facilier would be a Bata'a, who are the resident Voudoun practitioners of Mage: The Ascension. He'd perhaps also be an Infernalist, if he has debts to &quot;Friends on the other side&quot; he needs to pay. It's sort of hard to tell with Voudoun, whether the spirits being contacted are demons or just Loa. Depends on the interpretation.<br /> <br /> Spheres would be Spirit, Life, Time, and possibly Mind, as you said. He's shown the ability to create freaky visuals. If those are illusions (and not just non-diagetic visuals for the sake of the audience), it could use Mind or Forces, depending on whether the illusions were &quot;physical&quot;.<br /> <br /> His shadow tends to act independently of him, which might be a Forces effect, a Paradox Flaw, or even a shadow elemental as a Familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T20:45:27-07:00","id":1102180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1101991-dr-facilier-as-a-mage-how-it-could-be-done?p=1101999#post1101999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Facilier would be a Bata'a, who are the resident Voudoun practitioners of Mage: The Ascension. He'd perhaps also be an Infernalist, if he has debts to &quot;Friends on the other side&quot; he needs to pay. It's sort of hard to tell with Voudoun, whether the spirits being contacted are demons or just Loa. Depends on the interpretation.<br /> <br /> Spheres would be Spirit, Life, Time, and possibly Mind, as you said. He's shown the ability to create freaky visuals. If those are illusions (and not just non-diagetic visuals for the sake of the audience), it could use Mind or Forces, depending on whether the illusions were &quot;physical&quot;.<br /> <br /> His shadow tends to act independently of him, which might be a Forces effect, a Paradox Flaw, or even a shadow elemental as a Familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't believe I didn't think of the Bata'a... I am more used to the Traditions and Tecnocrats, but yeah, that's the best group. Well in Facilier's case yup, he was in a huge debt with his &quot;friends&quot; so he could be an infernalist.<br /> <br /> During the movie he also uses other shadows besides his own. All of them have this cool power of affecting anything by interacting with the shadow of it. You can see that in the video, whne Facilier's shadow takes off the two huys hats and again when it leans the chair... That looks awesome. So I don't know if there is a spirit that has a charm that could work that way...<br /> <br /> Still pretty nice suggestions. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T02:01:31-07:00","id":1102219,"title":"","content":"Yeah, looks like Bata'a (or voudoun orphan) concentrating on Spirit and Mind. I don't think he has forces or life spheres. Frog transformation was a favor from the spirit allies and he read the minds of clients to see their desires and fears, not a real divination. The animated shadow is presented in the Mage the Dark Ages. Best represented by spirit familiar merit. On the spirits I would say that they exist in dark penumbra but have shadows manifested in the real world. So a charm that allows for reaching through Gauntel should suffice (Reaching or Gauntlet Breach). Raccoon spirits can do something similar, it's a staple of trickster spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T01:58:30-07:00","id":1102738,"title":"","content":"It's a little tricky, because that movie seems to take place in a universe where the spirit world of the dead and the spirit world of banes are not distinct, but really just one thing. I'd say he's basically a Voudoun who has made a bargain with banes to create a powerful fetish. He's developed either paradox flaws, or the Echoes flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}